<ans># Aditya Birla Health Insurance Co Ltd — FY23 (Year Ended 31 March 2023) Financial Data Extraction

## Sourcing Note

The requested URL — `adityabirlacapital.com/healthinsurance/about-us/financials` — returns a **404 "Page Does Not Exist"** error and does not host any financial statements or IRDAI disclosure documents.

A follow-up search for Aditya Birla Health Insurance's (ABHI) FY23 IRDAI "NL" quarterly public disclosure set (NL-1 Revenue Account, NL-2 P&L, Balance Sheet) for the quarter/year ended March 2023 was unsuccessful. The only NL-form filing locatable on the company's domain is a **legacy filing for the quarter ended 31 December 2016**, which is out of period and unusable for FY23. No standalone statutory annual report or NL disclosure archive for FY23 was found on ABHI's public website, and the IRDAI portal did not surface a directly retrievable ABHI FY23 filing.

Given this, the table below is populated **only** with figures independently corroborated from **Aditya Birla Capital Ltd's (ABCL, ABHI's parent) Q4/FY23 consolidated results press release** — the only authoritative, dated, full-year document located that reports ABHI segment metrics. All other statutory line items (NWP, NEP, EoM ratio, commission ratio, net worth, AUM, solvency ratio, investment yield) could not be verified from any primary/statutory source and are left blank rather than estimated, per instructions.

## Extracted Data

| company | period | line_item | basis | value | unit | source_name | source_url | filing_date |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Aditya Birla Health Insurance Co Ltd | FY23 | Total GWP | IGAAP | **2717** | INR_crore | Aditya Birla Capital Ltd — Q4/FY23 Results Press Release | https://www.adityabirlacapital.com/-/media/ABCL/pdf/Quarterly-Results/Q4-FY23/Press-Release-Q4-FY23.ashx | 2023-05-11 |
| Aditya Birla Health Insurance Co Ltd | FY23 | Profit After Tax (PAT) | IGAAP | **-220** | INR_crore | Aditya Birla Capital Ltd — Q4/FY23 Results Press Release | https://www.adityabirlacapital.com/-/media/ABCL/pdf/Quarterly-Results/Q4-FY23/Press-Release-Q4-FY23.ashx | 2023-05-11 |
| Aditya Birla Health Insurance Co Ltd | FY23 | Combined ratio | IGAAP | **110** | % | Aditya Birla Capital Ltd — Q4/FY23 Results Press Release | https://www.adityabirlacapital.com/-/media/ABCL/pdf/Quarterly-Results/Q4-FY23/Press-Release-Q4-FY23.ashx | 2023-05-11 |

*(Rows for Retail health GWP, NWP, NEP, PAT-IFRS, Claims ratio, Expense ratio, EoM ratio, Commission ratio, Solvency ratio, Net worth, Retail health market share, AUM, and Investment yield have been omitted from the table above as no verifiable published value could be sourced for these line items.)*

## Key Findings & Data Gaps

- **GWP growth strong, retail-led:** ABHI's FY23 Gross Written Premium grew **57% YoY to ₹2,717 crore**, with **retail contributing 56%** of total business. This 56% figure is a disclosed *proportion*, not an audited absolute-value line item, so per the strict "no estimation" rule it has not been back-calculated into an absolute retail GWP value.

- **Underwriting profitability improving but still loss-making:** Combined ratio improved materially from **127% (FY22) to 110% (FY23)** — still above the 100% breakeven threshold, meaning underwriting losses persisted, consistent with a still-scaling standalone health insurer (SAHI) reinvesting in growth.

- **Net loss narrowing:** ABHI's standalone **net loss reduced ~29% to ₹220 crore in FY23 from ₹311 crore in FY22** — directionally positive (loss-shrinking trajectory) but confirms the company remained loss-making on a full-year IGAAP basis in FY23.

- **Market share gain (directional context only):** Market share among standalone health insurers (SAHI) rose **+208 bps YoY to 10.4% in FY23**. This is *overall* SAHI market share, not specifically "retail health market share" as requested, so it has not been populated in that exact row.

- **Critical sourcing gap — statutory/NL filings unavailable:** Net Written Premium, Net Earned Premium, Expense of Management ratio, Commission ratio, Net worth, AUM, Solvency ratio, and Investment yield for FY23 could **not** be sourced. ABHI's website hosts no FY23 IRDAI NL-1/NL-2/Balance Sheet disclosure archive (only a stale Dec-2016 filing exists), no FY23 standalone annual report was locatable, and the IRDAI portal did not surface a directly retrievable ABHI FY23 filing.

- **Third-party solvency figures conflict and are unreliable:** Aggregator sites cited divergent solvency ratios for ABHI as of March 2023 (one showing ~263%, another ~173%) — these are non-statutory secondary sources with internally inconsistent claims, so per source-hierarchy rules (statutory filings > web aggregators) this metric has not been populated to avoid propagating an unverified figure.

- **Corporate structure caveat impacting IFRS PAT:** ABHI ceased to be a subsidiary of ABCL in FY23 (following a preferential allotment to Platinum Jasmine A 2018 Trust/ADIA) and was reclassified as a joint venture, triggering a one-off fair-value gain of ₹2,739 crore at the **ABCL group** level. This is a parent-company consolidation gain, not an ABHI standalone IFRS PAT figure, and has correctly been excluded from the table to avoid conflating group-level one-offs with entity-level performance.

## Recommendation

To close the remaining data gaps (NWP, NEP, EoM ratio, net worth, AUM, solvency, investment yield), the next-best sources would be:
1. ABHI's FY23 audited standalone financial statements filed with the Registrar of Companies (MCA, CIN: U66000MH2015PLC263677), or
2. The IRDAI Annual Report/Handbook of Statistics for FY22-23

Both were outside the successfully retrievable document set in this research pass. If you have access to either of these documents, I'd be happy to extract the specific line items from them.</ans>
